The same question, 20 times, on gpt-5.4-mini.

  default               20 distinct answers of 20   most common appeared 1x
  temperature=0         20 distinct answers of 20   most common appeared 1x
  temperature=0 + seed  20 distinct answers of 20   most common appeared 1x

The steadiest setting still produced 20 different answers.

temperature=0 means 'always take the most likely token', and that is not the
same as 'always produce the same text'. Floating-point addition is not
associative, so a batch of a different size, a different GPU, or a different
kernel gives a different sum; when two tokens are nearly tied, a small
difference in the numbers decides which one wins, and every token after
it is downstream of that choice.

The seed changed nothing measurable here: 20 distinct answers without it,
20 with. A seed fixes the sampling, not the arithmetic, and it cannot fix a
provider that routed you to different hardware between two calls.

So the working assumption for the rest of this chapter is:

  the same input can produce a different output, on purpose-built
  infrastructure, with every knob set to its most deterministic value

Which means 'I cannot reproduce it' is not a diagnosis. It is the normal
condition, and §24.3 is about what you do instead.
